  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_strncasestr",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/ndpi_main.c",
    "description": "Heap out-of-bounds read in ndpi_strncasestr due to unsigned length underflow. The loop bound uses `i < (str1_len - str2_len + 1)` with `size_t`; when the searched buffer is shorter than the needle (e.g., Authorization header value length < 5 for \"Basic\" or < 6 for \"Digest\"), `str1_len - str2_len` underflows to a huge value. The function then keeps incrementing `str1` and reading past the end (`str1[0]` / `strncasecmp`), causing the ASan crash at line 7143. Crash is reached via check_content_type_and_change_protocol() calling ndpi_strncasestr() on `packet->authorization_line.ptr`.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_process_packet, attacker-controlled packet bytes are parsed as HTTP headers. If an `Authorization:` header is present, check_content_type_and_change_protocol() (http.c:728+) calls ndpi_strncasestr(authorization_value, \"Basic\", authorization_len) and again with \"Digest\". A short/malformed authorization value (as in the PoC) makes `authorization_len` smaller than the needle length, triggering size_t underflow in ndpi_strncasestr loop bound and an out-of-bounds read past the heap buffer."
  },
